    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** enter today with a clear emphasis on high-upside matchups, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our highest efficiency score of 81.88. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from an elite combination of a favorable hitter\u2019s park and a prime spot at the top of the order against Lugo, whose 4.53 xERA makes him a prime target for our leadoff man. Our next most reliable anchors are **Jacob Wilson** (71.63) and **Andy Pages** (71.40); **Jacob Wilson** draws a favorable tilt against Schultz (5.23 xERA), while **Andy Pages** is poised to exploit the matchup against Bratt, providing significant value even with his lineup position pending. We are also monitoring **Kyle Tucker** closely; despite his projected #6 spot in the order, his intrinsic talent and the platoon advantage against the lefty Bratt result in a stellar 75.35 efficiency rating.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s card involved **Brayan Rocchio**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a 56.28 score. While **Brayan Rocchio** benefits from a strong SP skill matchup against Phillips, his projected efficiency fell just shy of the threshold required to displace the high-scoring **Heliot Ramos** (63.48) or **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (70.23). Elsewhere, we continue to look for stolen base contributions from our speed-heavy roster; specifically, **Josh Lowe** and **Jackson Merrill** offer vital category-capping potential against slow-delivery pitchers, each receiving a +2% scoring bump for their high likelihood of successful swipes. We remain cautious with **Liam Hicks** (43.11), who sits just above our marginal threshold; his value is suppressed by a negative platoon shift against Cantillo, and he serves as our lowest-rated start. All managers should keep a sharp eye on the finalized lineups for **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Andy Pages**, and **Kyle Tucker**; any unexpected lineup drop-downs could necessitate a mid-day evaluation of our efficiency floor.",
